# UsArr — example environment file
#
# Copy to .env and edit.  `.env` is gitignored; NEVER commit a real key.
# Full reference: docs/CONFIGURATION.md
#
# STATUS: pre-alpha.  Some of these are live — the listener, URL base, data and
# config directories, logging, trusted proxies, the metadata User-Agent and the
# secret key are read by the binary today.  The rest are still the spec the
# implementation is being built to, and nothing reads them yet.
#
# UsArr's whole configuration surface is on this page.  Services — Sonarr,
# Radarr, Prowlarr, Jellyfin, Navidrome, metadata providers — are NOT configured
# here.  You add them in the UI, once, and they live encrypted in the database.
# There is no services.yaml, no config.yaml and no USARR_SONARR_URL.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Core process
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Irreplaceable state: the SQLite database, keys/, providers/, backups/.
# BACK THIS UP — but read docs/CONFIGURATION.md §6 first: `tar` of the whole
# directory puts the master key in the same file as the data it encrypts.
# Never place it on NFS/SMB — SQLite WAL needs real locking and shared memory.
USARR_CONFIG_DIR=/config

# Regenerable state: image cache, cache.db, logs, tmp.  Safe to delete.
# Defaults to USARR_CONFIG_DIR when unset (single-volume installs).
USARR_DATA_DIR=/data

# Interface to bind.  Use 127.0.0.1 when a reverse proxy runs on the same host.
USARR_BIND_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0

# HTTP listen port.  8484 avoids every default port UsArr talks to
# (8989/7878/8686/8787/9696/6969/5299/8096/32400/8080/6789/9091/8112/6767/5055).
USARR_PORT=8484

# Sub-path when reverse-proxied, e.g. https://home.example/usarr
# Leading slash, no trailing slash.  Must match the proxy exactly.  Empty = root.
USARR_URL_BASE=

# trace | debug | info | warn | error
# Credentials are redacted at EVERY level, `trace` included — a fixed deny-list
# of query parameters and auth headers is stripped by middleware before any log
# line exists.  See docs/CONFIGURATION.md §2.1.
USARR_LOG_LEVEL=info

# auto | text | json   (auto = text on a TTY, JSON otherwise)
USARR_LOG_FORMAT=auto

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Security — read docs/CONFIGURATION.md §3 before touching these
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# MASTER KEY.  Wraps the data-encryption keys protecting every stored service
# credential.  32 random bytes, base64.
#
# LEAVE IT COMMENTED OUT.  That is the correct, safe setting.  On first run
# UsArr generates a real key with real entropy into
# $USARR_CONFIG_DIR/keys/secret.key at mode 0600 and logs a line telling you to
# back it up.  A key you copy out of a file that is published in a git
# repository is not a key.
#
# Set it only if you want the key in a secrets manager instead of on the volume,
# and then prefer the _FILE form below.  Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# Startup fails, loudly and by name, if the value is empty, is not valid base64,
# does not decode to exactly 32 bytes, is all zeroes, or matches a placeholder
# ever shipped in this file.  There is no lenient fallback.
#
# Lose it and every stored service credential is unrecoverable — you re-paste
# each API key.  Your library, tags and requests survive intact.
#USARR_SECRET_KEY=
#USARR_SECRET_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/usarr_key

# CIDRs whose X-Forwarded-* headers are believed.  Needed ONLY behind a reverse
# proxy.  EMPTY MEANS TRUST NOTHING — the peer IP is used as-is.
# Set it to your proxy's network ONLY, never 0.0.0.0/0.  It gates rate-limit
# bucketing and the audit log's actor IP.
USARR_TRUSTED_PROXIES=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Metadata
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Contact string attached to outbound requests, and ONLY to the providers whose
# terms require or reward one: MusicBrainz (mandatory) and Open Library
# (1 -> 3 req/s).  Everything else gets a generic UsArr/<version>.
# NOTE: this value is transmitted to those third parties.  A project URL works
# as well as an email address.
#USARR_METADATA_USER_AGENT=UsArr/0.1 (+https://github.com/OWNER/UsArr)

# No provider API keys here.  TMDB, Fanart.tv, Comic Vine and the rest are
# configured in the UI and stored encrypted.  None of them is required to render
# your library at any milestone — the *Arrs already carry every field UsArr
# renders in v0.1.  See docs/CONFIGURATION.md §4.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Container
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# IANA timezone for logs, schedules and calendar rendering.
TZ=Etc/UTC

# There is no PUID/PGID/UMASK.  The image is distroless and runs as a fixed
# non-root UID (65532:65532) — it has no shell and cannot chown at startup.
# Pre-create and chown your volumes, or set `user:` in compose:
#   mkdir -p ./config ./data
#   sudo chown -R 65532:65532 ./config ./data && sudo chmod 700 ./config ./data
# See docs/CONFIGURATION.md §2.4.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Development only — not read in production builds
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Opt in to tests behind the `integration` build tag.  Requires a live stack;
# never set in CI (no Docker daemon there).  See docs/DEVELOPMENT.md §8.
#USARR_INTEGRATION=1

# Put go-vcr into record mode: real HTTP goes out and cassettes are written to
# testdata/cassettes/.  Secrets are scrubbed by a recorder hook before write.
#USARR_RECORD=1
